    "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements **ADR-027: @media Block Support** — @media block parsing + cascade-time viewport filtering. Three commits.\n\n**Honest framing:** this PR delivers **partial visible delta** — Wikipedia's navbox now shows structured section headers and colored backgrounds. The **layout transform the ADR hoped for (sidebar/header/TOC restructuring) does not ship** because the 106 layout-property declarations inside `@media` (`grid-template-columns`, `flex-*`, `column-*`, `float`, `position`) enter the cascade correctly but our **layout engine ignores them** (ADR-011 scoped layout to block + inline flow only).\n\n**What the PR delivers is real infrastructure** — 33 of 64 blocks fire at viewport 1024, cascade filtering works correctly, and the next layout-engine ADR will unlock the full structural transform without any further parser work.\n\n## What shipped\n\n### @media parser (Commit 1)\n\n- **`Rule` gains `optional<MediaQuery> media`**: nullopt = top-level rule, populated = @media-extracted.\n- **Prelude classifier**: `screen`/`all`/empty/`and`/`only` keywords; `(min-width: Npx)`; `(max-width: Npx)`; `calc(Npx ± Mpx)`; `and`-combinations.\n- **Unsupported preludes drop rules entirely**: `print`, `prefers-*`, `aspect-ratio`, `orientation`, `resolution`, `hover`, `pointer`, range syntax, mixed-unit calc. **Correct per CSS spec** — browser without the feature doesn't apply those rules.\n- **Nested @media inside blocks skipped** (0 nested cases on Wikipedia; safe drop per spec).\n- **15 tests** including both calc cases, all unsupported query types, multiple rules in one block, `@import` still skipped.\n- **Bug found during testing**: naive `find(')')` truncated calc conditions at inner parens (`calc(1120px - 1px)` became `calc(1120px - 1px` missing the trailing paren). Both calc tests failed, revealing the bug. Fixed with balanced-paren scan.\n\n### Cascade viewport filtering (Commit 2)\n\n- **`cascade()` gains `viewport_width` param** (default 1024 for backward compat — no existing tests break).\n- **`apply_rule()` early-returns on media mismatch** before running the selector match (cheap skip).\n- **`media_matches(mq, vw)` helper** — nullopt always matches; populated bounds must all satisfy.\n- **Threaded through** `compute_styles` → `cascade_subtree` → `RenderPipeline::relayout`.\n- **`RenderPipeline::last_viewport_width_`** stores the value for `restyle()`'s fallback path (correct because hover doesn't resize).\n- **7 tests** at viewports 500/1024/1500 covering min-width, max-width, calc, and-combinations, top-level rules, print-drop.\n\n### Measured visible delta on Wikipedia at viewport 1024\n\nScreenshots at three scroll positions vs. ADR-026 baseline:\n\n| Check | ADR-026 state | ADR-027 observed |\n|---|---|---|\n| CSS text hidden (display:none fix) | Gone | **Still gone** ✅ |\n| Article body readable | Yes | Yes ✅ |\n| References formatted | Yes | Yes ✅ |\n| **Wikipedia navbox** (bottom) | Plain list | **Structured section headers** (\"MSHTML\", \"WebKit\", \"Recommendations\") + **colored backgrounds** (light purple/blue tints on section boxes, tinted list items) ✅ **NEW** |\n| **Sidebar layout** | Vertical blob | Still vertical blob ❌ (grid/flex/column properties ignored by layout) |\n| **Header / TOC layout** | Text row / unstyled list | Unchanged ❌ |\n\n**The navbox win is real.** `@media { background-color: ... }` declarations winning cascade and being consumed by our paint layer. This is the first visible improvement from @media parsing.\n\n**Navboxes expanded = correct** — Wikipedia collapses navboxes via JS. We don't run JS, so expanded is semantically correct. A future JS-engine ADR would add collapse behavior.\n\n## The layout-engine gap (explicit)\n\n**106 layout-property declarations inside @media enter the cascade, 0 are consumed by `layout_element`.**\n\nADR-027's Context measured this before implementation (5.7% of declarations inside @media target grid/flex/column/float/position). Those declarations now cascade-win correctly. But `layout.cpp`'s `layout_element` doesn't read `grid-template-columns`, `flex-direction`, `column-width`, `float`, or `position`. The rule wins the cascade and the paint layer never sees it.\n\n**The full structural transform (sidebar shifts right, header bar layout, TOC position) requires a grid/flex/column layout-engine ADR.** That ADR is well-scoped: read the 5 layout properties we don't consume, implement basic grid/flex/column resolution in `layout_element`. When it lands, ADR-027's @media rules are already in the cascade with correct viewport gating — no further parser work needed.\n\n## The three-path Meta-lesson (progression from ADR-025 → 026 → 027)\n\n| Meta-lesson | ADR | Paths measured | Prediction miss |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| v1: measure the scale | 023 | Path 1 (parse) | \"2,500 `<a>` per wrapper not 10\" |\n| v2: trace the code path | 024 | Path 1+2 (parse + cascade-win) | Existing early-return skipped 17ms of work |\n| **v3: verify property-consumed** | **026, 027** | **All three** (parse + cascade-win + property-consumed) | ADR-026: negligible var() delta (path 3 failed for specificity reasons). ADR-027: navbox works (all three paths satisfied), sidebar doesn't (path 3 fails) |\n\n**Refined rule** (now documented in ADR-027's Implementation section):\n\n> To predict visible delta from any CSS subsystem, trace **three** paths: does it parse → does it win the cascade → does its winning property get consumed by paint/layout?\n\nADR-025 measured path 1 and got surprised by paths 2 and 3. ADR-026 measured 1+2 and got surprised by path 3. ADR-027 measured all three and its prediction (navbox visible, sidebar not) **matched reality**.\n\n## The six-ADR arc's honest state\n\n| ADR | Delivered | Visible delta | Followup |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 025 | External CSS loading | **Article content styled (~40-50%)** | Layout rules inside @media → ADR-027 |\n| 026 | var() resolution + display:none fix | Bug fix visible; **var() delta negligible** | Cascade loss → future specificity investigation |\n| 027 | @media parsing + cascade filtering | **Navbox styling visible**; layout transform deferred | grid/flex layout engine → future ADR |\n\n**The next visual-needle-mover is a layout-engine ADR**, not another CSS parser feature. ADR-027's infrastructure is complete and waiting for it.\n\n## Commits\n\n| Commit | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| `26a3078` | `MediaQuery` + `Rule.media` + prelude classifier + calc support. 14 tests. |\n| `90a5374` | Cascade viewport filtering + `viewport_width` threaded through. 7 tests. |\n| `a02e8e6` | Docs: ADR-027 status → Implemented, README, CHANGELOG, Meta-lesson-v3 refinement. |\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-027: 306 cases, 1297 assertions\n- After Commit 1: 320 cases, 1346 assertions (+14)\n- After Commit 2: **327 cases, 1367 assertions** (+7)\n- Zero warnings, zero failures\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| @media block extraction | ✅ (14 tests) |\n| calc(Npx ± Mpx) evaluated | ✅ (both sign cases tested) |\n| Unsupported queries drop rules | ✅ (print, prefers-*, mixed-unit calc, malformed) |\n| Cascade viewport filtering | ✅ (7 tests at 500/1024/1500) |\n| `min-width: 1120` does NOT fire at 1024 | ✅ |\n| `max-width: calc(1120px - 1px)` fires at 1024 | ✅ (critical Wikipedia case) |\n| Existing tests (no viewport set) unchanged | ✅ (default 1024 preserves behavior) |\n| **Visible delta** | ⚠️ **partial** — navbox yes, layout no (honest, documented) |\n| No regression | ✅ |\n\n## Not included (deferred)\n\n- Recursive `@media` (0 nested cases on Wikipedia)\n- `prefers-color-scheme`, `prefers-reduced-motion`, `prefers-contrast`\n- `@media print` (no print rendering yet)\n- Complex queries (`aspect-ratio`, `orientation`, `resolution`, `hover`, `pointer`, range syntax)\n- `calc()` with mixed units (`calc(50% - 20px)`)\n- Nested `@media` blocks\n- **Grid/flex/column layout engine** — the ADR that fully unlocks the Vector structural transform (106 declarations inside @media target these; layout engine doesn't consume them)\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/027-media-queries.md` — status now **Implemented**, with Implementation section documenting the navbox visible win, the layout-engine gap, and the three-path Meta-lesson refinement.\n\nRefs #157\n",
